\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371386 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371387 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371388 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$"] [:db/cas 17592186371388 :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-6I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-6I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186371390 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371391 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371392 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371393 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186371394 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{