{aligned}],\\,{Σ}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}],\\,{V}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" "$$\n{U}_{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}_{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{26}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{V}_{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186371810 :question/worked-solution "If $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}_{r}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of ${Σ}_{r}.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}],\\,{U}_{r}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "If $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}_{r}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of ${Σ}_{r}.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}_{r}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186371812 :answer/value "\\frac{1}{52}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\frac{1}{52}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186371813 :answer/value "\\frac{1}{104}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\frac{1}{104}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186371814 :answer/value "\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" "\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186371815 :answer/value "\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186371816 :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" "\\frac{1}{13}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186371817 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$*