iple linear regression as \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?"] [:db/cas 17592186373771 :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$8$** | **$12$** | **$17$** |\n| ${x}_{3}$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$6$** | **$10$** | **$15$** |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\n \n\nThe coefficients of the hyperplane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}_{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 17 & 15\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$8$** | **$12$** | **$17$** |\n| ${x}_{3}$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$6$** | **$10$** | **$15$** |\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\n \n\nThe coefficients of the hyperplane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}_{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 17 & 15\\end{bmatr